  "knowledgePattern": "Recover a signed trigonometric product from a tangent value",
  "knowledgeTags": [
    "trigonometry"
  ],
  "solution": "<p>Tangent is positive in the first and third quadrants. The given interval excludes the first, so both sine and cosine are negative.</p><p>A reference triangle with opposite side 2 and adjacent side 1 has hypotenuse <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow></math>. Therefore <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>.</p><p>The product is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></math>. Answer A.</p>",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Find the quadrant",
      "body": "<p>Sketch the axes. Within the stated angle interval, mark where tangent is positive.</p>",
      "recap": "Tangent is positive when sine and cosine have the same sign.",
      "pitfall": "A positive tangent does not mean sine and cosine are positive.",
      "pause": "Work out the signs of sine and cosine in the allowed quadrant.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l16",
          "reminder": "Tangent is positive when sine and cosine have the same sign."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Draw a right triangle",
      "body": "<p>Use a reference triangle whose opposite-to-adjacent ratio is 2 to 1. Find its hypotenuse with Pythagoras, then use it to find the sizes of sine and cosine.</p>",
      "recap": "In a right triangle, sine is opposite over hypotenuse and cosine is adjacent over hypotenuse.",
      "pitfall": "The triangle gives the sizes; the quadrant gives the signs.",
      "pause": "Put the correct signs on both ratios, then multiply them.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-extra-right-triangle-ratios",
          "reminder": "In a right triangle, sine is opposite over hypotenuse and cosine is adjacent over hypotenuse."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
